This file gathers and re-exports the combinators of Theorem 5.6 (Scott 1981, PRG-19): the strict identity and the strict first projection, the four selectors on a function space paired with an argument pair, the body, operator, and least fixed point of primitive recursion, and the body, operator, least fixed point, and map of the μ-scheme. The theorem states that every partial recursive function on the natural-number domain is denoted by a λ-term built from the conditional, successor, predecessor, the zero test, and zero, by closure under composition, primitive recursion, and the least-number operator.
